`storage gen` (#393) plans the router's storages from a small deployment file
— the RFC 09 §2 block, with the thing a human types wrong derived instead:
`strip_prefix` as the literal leftmost run of the selector. Each storage names
its selector, relative to the deployment namespace; a lifespan is the file's,
or zenoh's 24 h default, and says which — a zk2 contract declares no
tombstone lifetime to derive one from. v1's class table and the registry
`ttl_s` its lifespans were derived from left at FJ9 (#612).

The plan opens no session: only `--check` asks a router anything.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --format table
storage plan for namespace "fleet-a"

volumes:
  fs        fs        durable · latest
  influxdb  influxdb  durable · all     url="http://localhost:8086"

storages:
  events      fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**       fs (latest)     replicated, complete
    strip fleet-a/zk2
    gc lifespan 86400 s (period 30 s): zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from
    ! overlap: overlaps links (fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
  links       fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/**  fs (latest)
    strip fleet-a/zk2
    gc lifespan 3600 s (period 30 s): declared gc_lifespan_s 3600
    ! overlap: overlaps events (fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
  plant       fleet-a/plant/**                  influxdb (all)
    strip fleet-a/plant
    gc lifespan 86400 s (period 30 s): zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from
    ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
  timeseries  fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/stream/**       influxdb (all)
    strip fleet-a/zk2
    gc lifespan 86400 s (period 30 s): zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from
    ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
4 storage(s) on 2 volume(s) planned, 0 refused
`--json5` emits the zenohd plugins.storage_manager block; `--check` compares it with what a router runs; `--explain <key>` says which storage takes a key

```

`--json5` is the file: the `plugins.storage_manager` block `zenohd` reads, with
every derivation and warning as a comment beside the storage it concerns. A
foreign schema, so it is a flag of its own and not a `--format` (#243).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --json5
// zenohd storage_manager block — generated by `zenctl storage gen` (RFC 09 §2).
// namespace "fleet-a".
// Merge under the router config's `plugins`; every non-memory volume needs its backend plugin installed, version-matched to the router.
plugins: {
  storage_manager: {
    volumes: {
      fs: {},  // durable · latest (RFC 09 §2.1)
      influxdb: { url: "http://localhost:8086" },  // durable · all (RFC 09 §2.1)
    },
    storages: {
      // events
      // ! overlap: overlaps links (fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
      events: {
        key_expr: "fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**",
        strip_prefix: "fleet-a/zk2",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "fs", dir: "events" },
        replication: { hot: 6, interval: 10.0, propagation_delay: 250, sub_intervals: 5, warm: 30 },  // identical on every replica (RFC 09 §2.2)
        complete: true,  // replicated latest-mode storage (RFC 09 §2.2)
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 86400 },  // zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // links
      // ! overlap: overlaps events (fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**): a GET under both selectors is answered by both, duplicate and possibly divergent — accept it (subscribers are unaffected; GET consumers consolidate) or carve one selector out of the other (RFC 09 §2)
      links: {
        key_expr: "fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/**",
        strip_prefix: "fleet-a/zk2",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "fs", dir: "links" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 3600 },  // declared gc_lifespan_s 3600 (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // plant
      // ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
      plant: {
        key_expr: "fleet-a/plant/**",
        strip_prefix: "fleet-a/plant",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "influxdb", db: "plant" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 86400 },  // zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
      // timeseries
      // ! retention_is_the_databases: retention is the database's policy (an InfluxDB retention policy), not zenoh config: garbage_collection prunes metadata and never drops a value, so this storage's data grows until the database prunes it — size the volume against the write rate (RFC 09 §2.3)
      timeseries: {
        key_expr: "fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/stream/**",
        strip_prefix: "fleet-a/zk2",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "influxdb", db: "streams" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 86400 },  // zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
    },
  },
}
4 storage(s) on 2 volume(s) planned, 0 refused

```

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --json5 --format json
? 2
error: the argument '--json5' cannot be used with '--format <FORMAT>'

--json5 emits a foreign document format — somebody else's schema — while --format chooses among zenctl's own three renderings of a report. Drop one.

Usage: zenctl <COMMAND>

For more information, try '--help'.

```

`--explain <key>` is pure over the plan: which storage takes the key, and
why — and, for a key in a verbatim chunk, why `events` does not (`*` and `**`
never match an `@`-chunk, RFC 03 §4 D2/D4).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --format table --explain 'fleet-a/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/events/link/01k0'
fleet-a/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/events/link/01k0
  → events  fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**       includes it
      its selector under namespace "fleet-a": fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/** includes every key fleet-a/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/events/link/01k0 names; stored under strip_prefix "fleet-a/zk2" on volume fs (latest)
  → links   fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/**  includes it
      its selector under namespace "fleet-a": fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/link/** includes every key fleet-a/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/events/link/01k0 names; stored under strip_prefix "fleet-a/zk2" on volume fs (latest)

```

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --format table --explain 'fleet-a/zk2/host-a/cam/video.v1/@stream/frames'
fleet-a/zk2/host-a/cam/video.v1/@stream/frames
  none: no planned storage's selector includes it — it holds a verbatim chunk (`@…`), and `*`/`**` never match one: a storage must name it

```

A refusal names the storage and leaves the rest of the plan standing. Three
here, each for its own reason: replication on an all-mode volume is what the
storage manager refuses at startup (§2.2), so the plan refuses first; a volume
nobody declared; a selector that is not a key expression. With nothing left
to emit, `gen` exits 2: the input was refused whole, and an act with nothing
to do has no 1 to give.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages-refused.toml --format ndjson
? 2
{"base":"fleet-a","notes":[{"text":"refused storage history: declares replication on volume /"influxdb/", whose history mode is all — the storage manager refuses to start such a storage, so this plan refuses it first (anti-entropy aligns one value per key; an all-mode volume cannot participate) (RFC 09 §2.2)"},{"text":"refused storage stray: names volume /"rocks/", which [volumes] does not declare (RFC 09 §2)"},{"text":"refused storage typo: /"fleet-a/zk2//events/" is not a valid key expression (RFC 03 §2)"}],"report":"storage-plan"}
{"history":"all","id":"influxdb","persistence":"durable","plugin":"influxdb","row":"volume"}
{"cite":"RFC 09 §2.2","key_expr":"fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/stream/**","reason":"declares replication on volume /"influxdb/", whose history mode is all — the storage manager refuses to start such a storage, so this plan refuses it first (anti-entropy aligns one value per key; an all-mode volume cannot participate)","row":"refusal","storage":"history"}
{"cite":"RFC 09 §2","key_expr":"fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/events/**","reason":"names volume /"rocks/", which [volumes] does not declare","row":"refusal","storage":"stray"}
{"cite":"RFC 03 §2","key_expr":"fleet-a/zk2//events","reason":"/"fleet-a/zk2//events/" is not a valid key expression","row":"refusal","storage":"typo"}
refused storage history: declares replication on volume "influxdb", whose history mode is all — the storage manager refuses to start such a storage, so this plan refuses it first (anti-entropy aligns one value per key; an all-mode volume cannot participate) (RFC 09 §2.2)
refused storage stray: names volume "rocks", which [volumes] does not declare (RFC 09 §2)
refused storage typo: "fleet-a/zk2//events" is not a valid key expression (RFC 03 §2)
Error: every storage was refused — nothing to emit (the refusals are above)

```

A deployment file that still names a v1 class is refused by the parser, with
serde's own wording naming the field — exit 2, the input refused.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages-v1.toml
? 2
Error: --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages-v1.toml: TOML parse error at line 9, column 1
  |
9 | class = "state"
  | ^^^^^
unknown field `class`, expected one of `selector`, `volume`, `params`, `replication`, `complete`, `retention`, `gc_period_s`, `gc_lifespan_s`

```

`--check` is a verdict verb: a session that will not open lands on the
reserved 2, never on the 1 that would claim a difference this run never
measured (`zenctl/src/exit.rs`).

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storages.toml --check --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
storage gen --check: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A deployment file this tool cannot read is its input refused — exit 2, with
serde's own wording naming the key it did not know.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-deployment.toml
? 2
Error: --deployment: cannot read tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-deployment.toml: No such file or directory (os error 2)

```

## From the enrollment (#704)

`--enrollment` reads the enrollment `acl gen` reads, and the contracts its
services implement: a **union storage** per event resource (spec §2.6), keyed
`zk2/*/*/<iface>/events/<template>/<ulid>`, its lifespan the contract's
`retention`. The tcgui pilot's backends implement three interfaces, and only
`tc.netem.v1` declares an event; nothing is planned on any owner's state (S4).
With no `[events]` volume named, the union storage uses zenoh's memory backend,
and the plan says it is volatile.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --format table
storage plan for namespace ""

volumes:
  memory  memory  volatile · latest
    ! implicit_volume: no deployment file names an [events] volume, so the union storages derived from the enrollment use zenoh's memory backend: volatile, every stored occurrence is lost on a router restart — name one with `[events] volume = …` in --deployment (RFC 09 §2.1)

storages:
  events-tc.netem.v1-applied  zk2/*/*/tc.netem.v1/events/applied/*  memory (latest)
    union storage for tc.netem.v1 events/applied, implemented by h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc, h-20609002f7b6/tc
    strip zk2
    gc lifespan 604800 s (period 30 s): the contract's retention for tc.netem.v1 events/applied, 7d (604800 s, spec §2.6): a tombstone is kept as long as an occurrence may be replayed
    ! retention_not_enforced: the contract's retention (7d) bounds a replay, not this storage: garbage_collection prunes tombstones and never an occurrence, and the memory backend ignores `_time` (spike S5) — a consumer replays with a GET bounded by the retention, enforced by a time-series backend or its own filter (spec §2.6)
from the enrollment: 1 union storage(s), one per event resource of an interface an enrolled service implements; none on an owner's state/** or @state/** — current state is the owner's, last-known an archive's (spec §2.6, §4.2 S4)
tc.netif.v1, tc.scenario.v1 declare(s) no event resource: nothing of theirs is a storage's to keep
1 storage(s) on 1 volume(s) planned, 0 refused
`--json5` emits the zenohd plugins.storage_manager block; `--check` compares it with what a router runs; `--explain <key>` says which storage takes a key

```

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --json5
// zenohd storage_manager block — generated by `zenctl storage gen` (RFC 09 §2).
// namespace "".
// Merge under the router config's `plugins`; every non-memory volume needs its backend plugin installed, version-matched to the router.
// Union storages derived from an enrollment: one per event resource (spec §2.6). None on an owner's state/** or @state/** (spec §4.2 S4).
plugins: {
  storage_manager: {
    volumes: {
      // ! implicit_volume: no deployment file names an [events] volume, so the union storages derived from the enrollment use zenoh's memory backend: volatile, every stored occurrence is lost on a router restart — name one with `[events] volume = …` in --deployment (RFC 09 §2.1)
      memory: {},  // volatile · latest (RFC 09 §2.1)
    },
    storages: {
      // events-tc.netem.v1-applied
      // union storage for tc.netem.v1 events/applied (spec §2.6), implemented by h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc, h-20609002f7b6/tc
      // ! retention_not_enforced: the contract's retention (7d) bounds a replay, not this storage: garbage_collection prunes tombstones and never an occurrence, and the memory backend ignores `_time` (spike S5) — a consumer replays with a GET bounded by the retention, enforced by a time-series backend or its own filter (spec §2.6)
      "events-tc.netem.v1-applied": {
        key_expr: "zk2/*/*/tc.netem.v1/events/applied/*",
        strip_prefix: "zk2",  // derived: the literal leftmost run of key_expr
        volume: { id: "memory" },
        garbage_collection: { period: 30, lifespan: 604800 },  // the contract's retention for tc.netem.v1 events/applied, 7d (604800 s, spec §2.6): a tombstone is kept as long as an occurrence may be replayed (RFC 09 §2.3)
      },
    },
  },
}
from the enrollment: 1 union storage(s), one per event resource of an interface an enrolled service implements; none on an owner's state/** or @state/** — current state is the owner's, last-known an archive's (spec §2.6, §4.2 S4)
tc.netif.v1, tc.scenario.v1 declare(s) no event resource: nothing of theirs is a storage's to keep
1 storage(s) on 1 volume(s) planned, 0 refused

```

The event resources and their retentions are the contracts', so an enrollment
without `--contracts` is refused — exit 2 — and so is a run given neither
input.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml
? 2
Error: --enrollment needs --contracts: the event resources and their retentions are the contracts'

```

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --format table
? 2
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  <--enrollment <FILE>|--deployment <FILE>>

Usage: zenctl storage gen --format <FORMAT> --namespace <NS> <--enrollment <FILE>|--deployment <FILE>>

For more information, try '--help'.

```

## Never on owners' state (S4)

A deployment file's selector that intersects an owner's `state/**` or
`@state/**` is refused, citing spec §4.2 S4: a storage there would answer GETs
on an owner's state. The plan is shown — the refusal is in it, and the foreign
`plant/**` beside it is planned — and the run exits 2: a storage on owners'
state is input this tool refuses, not a caveat to emit around.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/state.toml --format table
? 2
storage plan for namespace "fleet-a"

volumes:
  fs  fs  durable · latest

storages:
  plant  fleet-a/plant/**  fs (latest)
    strip fleet-a/plant
    gc lifespan 86400 s (period 30 s): zenoh's default 86400 s — no contract declares a tombstone lifetime to derive one from
refused storage latest: "fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/state/**" intersects owners' state keys (`fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/state/**`): a storage there would answer GETs on an owner's state, which a deployment MUST NOT run — current state is the owner's answer, and last-known state an archive.v1's (§4.4) (spec §4.2 S4)
1 storage(s) on 1 volume(s) planned, 1 refused
`--json5` emits the zenohd plugins.storage_manager block; `--check` compares it with what a router runs; `--explain <key>` says which storage takes a key
Error: storage latest would answer on owners' state keys: a deployment MUST NOT run a storage there (spec §4.2 S4) — current state is the owner's answer, and last-known state an archive's (§4.4)

```

## `--check --against`, as `acl gen` has it

A router config file, read through zenoh's own loader: what is compared is what
`zenohd` would run, and no session is opened. Clean, exit 0:

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --check --against tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router.json5 --format table
storage check for namespace "" against tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router.json5: 1 planned, 1 observed row(s) — clean — tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router.json5 configures every planned storage as planned, and nothing else
compared with tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router.json5 as zenoh's loader reads it — what zenohd would run, not what a router runs now

```

Drifted, exit 1: the audit storage keeps tombstones for zenoh's default 24 h,
below the contract's 7 d retention, and a storage nobody planned answers on
owners' state — `extra`, and S4's finding beside it, planned or not.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --check --against tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router-drifted.json5 --format table
? 1
storage check for namespace "" against tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router-drifted.json5: 1 planned, 2 observed row(s) — 3 finding(s)
  ✗ events-tc.netem.v1-applied  gc.lifespan below the plan's  planned 604800, observed 86400
  ✗ latest                      extra                         observed zk2/*/*/*/state/**
  ✗ latest                      on owners' state (S4)         observed zk2/*/*/*/state/** (intersects `zk2/*/*/*/state/**`, spec §4.2 S4)
compared with tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router-drifted.json5 as zenoh's loader reads it — what zenohd would run, not what a router runs now

```

A plan that refused a storage on owners' state is not a question to put: the
check is the reserved 2.

```console
$ zenctl storage gen --deployment tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/state.toml --check --against tests/cmd/fixtures/storage/router.json5
? 2
refused storage latest: "fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/state/**" intersects owners' state keys (`fleet-a/zk2/*/*/*/state/**`): a storage there would answer GETs on an owner's state, which a deployment MUST NOT run — current state is the owner's answer, and last-known state an archive.v1's (§4.4) (spec §4.2 S4)
Error: storage latest would answer on owners' state keys: a deployment MUST NOT run a storage there (spec §4.2 S4) — current state is the owner's answer, and last-known state an archive's (§4.4)
storage gen --check: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
